BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Pawnshop Lockers) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY) Tj T* () Tj T* (Pawnshop Lockers) Tj T* (Submitted to the University Business Plan Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (OVERVIEW) Tj T* () Tj T* (Pawnshop Lockers is a early stage Internet and Consumer Technology company that is building a) Tj T* (network of smart-lock parcel lockers placed inside corner stores and laundromats in apartment) Tj T* (heavy neighborhoods. Our mission is to be the trusted last step for packages in places where) Tj T* (the traditional delivery model is broken. We combine electronic hardware, a mobile app, and) Tj T* (local business partnerships into one solution that we believe is disruptive and scalable.) Tj T* () Tj T* (THE PROBLEM) Tj T* () Tj T* (Package theft is a huge problem in the United States. Millions of packages are stolen every) Tj T* (year according to various surveys we have read, and the problem is especially bad in dense) Tj T* (apartment neighborhoods where buildings dont have a doorman, a secure mailroom, or even a) Tj T* (working front door lock. Packages get left in hallways, on stoops, or in lobbies where anyone) Tj T* (can take them. Residents in these neighborhoods often work long or irregular hours so they cant) Tj T* (be home to receive deliveries. When a package is stolen the customer has to deal with the) Tj T* (retailer, wait for a replacement, and lose trust in online shopping. Several of our team) Tj T* (members have personally had packages stolen in the apartments they lived in while at school,) Tj T* (which is how we got the idea.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Existing solutions like the lockers in big chain stores and in some apartment lobbies are not) Tj T* (available in the neighborhoods that need them most, because those neighborhoods have older) Tj T* (buildings and lower income residents and are not a priority for large companies.) Tj T* () Tj T* (OUR SOLUTION) Tj T* () Tj T* (We install a modular locker unit inside a local corner store or laundromat. The unit has a) Tj T* (cellular connected smart lock on each compartment, so it doesnt need the shops wifi. A resident) Tj T* (signs up on our app, gets a Pawnshop Lockers address code, and uses it at checkout so their) Tj T* (package is sent to the locker. When it arrives, the resident receives a notification and a one) Tj T* (time pickup code. They walk to the shop, enter the code, and the door opens. The shop owner) Tj T* (does not have to handle any packages, which keeps their workload low, and they earn a fee each) Tj T* (time a package is picked up.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The name comes from the idea that the neighborhood shop is a trusted place that people already) Tj T* (visit, like a pawnshop used to be a neighborhood anchor. We think this brand is memorable.) Tj T* () Tj T* (THE MARKET) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are many apartment dwellers in America, and e-commerce keeps growing every year. If even) Tj T* (a small percent of these households used a locker near them, the market would be very large. We) Tj T* (estimate that there are tens of thousands of corner stores and laundromats in the target type) Tj T* (of neighborhood nationwide, and if each had a locker at a modest fee the revenue potential is) Tj T* (in the billions. Our initial target is a few neighborhoods in our city, then other cities with) Tj T* (similar density. We have not yet done a formal market sizing but we believe the top down) Tj T* (numbers are very promising.) Tj T* () Tj T* (BUSINESS MODEL) Tj T* () Tj T* (We make money in a few ways. First, we charge a fee per package pickup, part of which is passed) Tj T* (to the shop owner as their commission. Second, we plan to charge residents a small optional) Tj T* (subscription for extended storage time and text alerts. Third, we plan to partner with delivery) Tj T* (carriers and retailers who would pay us to use the lockers as a delivery destination, and with) Tj ET
endstream
